From 629cf8824c760febecfa9e68dce1ad58b338fad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Tada Antunes <leonardotada@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:24:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] SATB foundation: release barrier for
 free/realloc/removeRoots

Adds d.gc.satb: a global marking flag, a per-thread buffer, a global queue and
satbShadeRange. While the flag is set, releasing a block (free, destroy, a
realloc that moves or shrinks) and removing a root range log every pointer they
delete, and thread exit flushes the buffer. These are the non-store deletions
found by the protocol model (free needs the deletion barrier; removeRoot too).

The flag is never set by the stop-the-world collector, so behaviour is
unchanged. The concurrent mark phase will set it and drain the queue.

Unit tests cover each hook and fail when it is disabled.
---
 source/d/gc/global.d |  34 ++++++
 source/d/gc/satb.d   | 256 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 source/d/gc/tcache.d | 148 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 438 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 source/d/gc/satb.d

